{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction","lean:module:QOU.Mass.InvolutionNumbers","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence"],"declarations":36,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.kernel_jacobi_beta_one_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.kernel_jacobi_beta_one_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":440,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L440-L445","doc":"At `v = 1` (`q = 1`) the kernel frame's `β₁` is the monic-Laguerre\n`β₁ = 1²  = 1` — the determinate archimedean (`e^{−s}ds`) pin. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.kernel_jacobi_beta_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.kernel_jacobi_beta_one","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L427-L438","doc":"**The kernel frame's first Jacobi coefficient** (audit §3 finding 1):\n`β₁ = m₂ − m₁² = v + v⁻¹ − 1 = 1 + (v − 1)²·v⁻¹` — the Wenzl quantity\n`q^{1/2} + q^{−1/2} − 1`, with the audit's sum-of-squares positivity shape\n(`β₁ − 1 = (v−1)²/v`) exact in the half-variable. This is the entire\ngeneral-`k` kernel-frame content the audit derives (no closed form exists\nbeyond `k = 1` there — honest residual, see module docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.balancedNormalizer_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.balancedNormalizer_three","kind":"theorem","line":417,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L417-L425","doc":"The second balanced kernel moment in the half-variable `v = q^{1/2}`:\n`m₂ = N^bal(3) = v⁻¹·[2]_{v²} = v + v⁻¹` — i.e. `q^{1/2} + q^{−1/2}`, the\nWenzl positivity quantity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.balancedNormalizer_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.balancedNormalizer_two","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L410-L415","doc":"The first balanced kernel moment is `1`:\n`m₁ = N^bal(2) = balancedNormalizer v 2 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_q_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_q_one","kind":"theorem","line":394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L394-L405","doc":"At `q = 1` the carrier moments ARE the involution numbers\n`I(n) = QOU.Mass.involutionNumber n` — the moments of the Gaussian\n`N(1,1)` (audit §3: the classical fibre of the q-deformed Gaussian). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_q_one_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_q_one_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L386-L392","doc":"At `q = 1` the carrier recurrence is Stein's characterization of the\nGaussian: `S(n+2) = S(n+1) + (n+1)·S(n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiBeta_q_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiBeta_q_one","kind":"theorem","line":381,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L381-L384","doc":"At `q = 1` the Jacobi off-diagonal degenerates to the Gaussian\n`β_{k+1} = k + 1` (i.e. `β_j = j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiAlpha_q_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiAlpha_q_one","kind":"theorem","line":378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L378-L379","doc":"At `q = 1` the Jacobi diagonal degenerates to the Gaussian `α_k = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_zero_eq_of_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_zero_eq_of_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L367-L374","doc":"Hypothesis-style form matching `keystone_bridge_binding_qlift`: for ANY\nsequence `S` with the q-involution recurrence and standard seed, the Jacobi\nmoments reproduce `S` — `(Mⁿ)₀₀ = S(n)` for every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_zero_eq_carrierMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_zero_eq_carrierMoment","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L358-L365","doc":"**The GNS moment identity at general `n`** (the audit's queued\ngeneral-`k` statement, closed): `(Mⁿ)₀₀ = S_q(n)` — the canonical monic\nJacobi operator with carrier data `α_k = q^k`, `β_k = q^{k−1}[k]_q` has\nthe q-involution carrier sequence as its moments, for EVERY `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_eq_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_eq_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L275-L356","doc":"**THE MAIN INDUCTION (general `k`, sorry-free).** The full closed form\nfor the iterated Jacobi vector of the carrier data `α_k = q^k`,\n`β_k = q^{k−1}[k]_q`:\n\n  `(Mⁿe₀)_i = q^{C(i,2)} · [m+1]_q[m+2]_q⋯[m+i]_q · S_q(m)`,  `n = i + m`.\n\nThe induction on `n` consumes exactly (i) the q-integer splitting\n`qint_add` and (ii) the q-involution recurrence of `carrierMoment` — the\nq-Stein identity. This is the general-`k` closure of the probe's K1\nverified-range identity (audit §5 item 1, queued there, discharged here). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_eq_zero_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_eq_zero_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L259-L273","doc":"Vanishing above the diagonal: `(Mⁿe₀)_i = 0` for `i > n` (the Jacobi\nmatrix moves the top entry down at most one level per step). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.choose_two_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.choose_two_succ","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L253-L255","doc":"`C(i+1,2) = i + C(i,2)` — the exponent step for the `q^{C(i,2)}` weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qRise_succ_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qRise_succ_left","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L243-L251","doc":"Bottom extraction: `[m+1]⋯[m+i+1] = [m+1]·([m+2]⋯[m+i+1])`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qRise_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qRise_one","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L239-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qRise_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qRise_succ","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L236-L237","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qRise_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qRise_zero","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L234-L234","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qRise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qRise","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L225-L232","doc":"`qRise q m i = [m+1]_q·[m+2]_q⋯[m+i]_q` — the `i`-step rising product,\nthe subtraction-free form of the falling factorial `[n]_q⋯[n−i+1]_q` at\n`n = m + i`. (`[i]_q!·qbinom(n,i) = qRise q (n−i) i`, so the closed form\nbelow is the q-binomial form `c(n,i) ∝ qbinom(n,i)·S(n−i)` with the\nweight `q^{C(i,2)}·[i]_q!` absorbed.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_succ_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_succ_succ","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L217-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_succ_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_succ_zero","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L213-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_zero_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_zero_succ","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L210-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_zero_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec_zero_zero","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L208-L208","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiVec","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L202-L206","doc":"`jacobiVec q n i = (Mⁿe₀)_i` — the iterated Jacobi vector. Its top\nentry `jacobiVec q n 0 = (Mⁿ)₀₀` is the GNS moment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiStep","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L194-L200","doc":"One application of the monic Jacobi matrix `M` (diagonal `α_i`,\nsuperdiagonal `1`, subdiagonal `β_i`) to a coordinate vector — the probe's\n`monic_jacobi_pow00` step: `(Mv)_i = β_i·v_{i−1} + α_i·v_i + v_{i+1}`,\nwith the `β`-term absent at `i = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiBeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiBeta","kind":"def","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L188-L192","doc":"**Jacobi off-diagonal** — `jacobiBeta q k` is `β_{k+1} = q^k·[k+1]_q`,\nthe probe's `betas[k]`; index-shifted by one so the audit's\n`β_j = q^{j−1}[j]_q` (`j ≥ 1`) is subtraction-free (`j = k+1`). `q = 1`\nlimit: the Gaussian `β_j = j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiAlpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.jacobiAlpha","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L184-L186","doc":"**Jacobi diagonal** `α_k = q^k` (audit §3, carrier frame; `q = 1`\nlimit: the Gaussian `α_k = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_unique","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L168-L180","doc":"**Uniqueness of the carrier sequence**: any sequence with the\nq-involution recurrence and initial values `1, 1` — i.e. any sequence\nadmissible in `keystone_bridge_binding_qlift` with the standard seed — is\n`carrierMoment`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_succ_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_succ_succ","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L163-L166","doc":"The defining q-involution (q-Stein) recurrence, as a rewrite lemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_index_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_index_one","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L161-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment_zero","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L159-L159","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.carrierMoment","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L147-L157","doc":"**The carrier moments** `S_q(n)`: the q-involution numerators of the\nLean-proved binding recurrence (`S(0) = S(1) = 1`,\n`S(n+2) = S(n+1) + [n+1]_q·S(n)`) — exactly the sequence hypothesis of\n`QOU.Mass.KeystoneBridgeC1Binding.keystone_bridge_binding_qlift`, made\nconcrete. Read as a Hamburger moment sequence (KSel-2 carrier frame). At\n`q = 1` these are the involution numbers `I(n)`, the moments of the\nGaussian `N(1,1)` (`carrierMoment_q_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qfact_index_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qfact_index_two","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L140-L143","doc":"`[2]_q! = [2]_q = 1 + q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qfact_index_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qfact_index_one","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L133-L138","doc":"`[m]_q!` at index `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qint_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qint_add","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L121-L131","doc":"**The q-integer splitting** `[a+b]_q = [a]_q + q^a·[b]_q` — the single\nalgebraic identity driving the main induction (it is the `i ≤ n` case of\nthe classical `[n+1]_q = [i]_q + q^i·[n+1−i]_q`, stated subtraction-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qint_one_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qint_one_val","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L118-L119","doc":"`[1]_q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qint_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedCarrierJacobi.qint_succ","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedCarrierJacobi.lean#L113-L116","doc":"One-step unfolding of the one-sided quantum integer:\n`[k+1]_q = [k]_q + q^k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}